/-
# LinnikContract — Numerics.lean

The numerics of `ROUTE_LEAD.md` §4, in explicit rational form.

`Area7` (`Assembly`) needs the numerical inequality of HB Lemma 15.1 at `L = 11/2`, `K = 3/10`,
and the §14 inequality of HB Lemma 14.1.  This file makes those numerical inputs **explicit
rational parameters** and certifies the closing inequalities with `norm_num`.

* Every transcendental quantity is replaced by an explicit rational enclosure with outward
  rounding to 10 decimals (`e^{-aλ}`, `e^{-2Kλ}`, `e^{-Kλ}`, `e^{-(73/30)λ}`, `e^{-(41/30)λ}`).
  The enclosures are *not* proved here (that is interval arithmetic on `Real.exp`), but they are
  literal rational data, so that everything downstream is pure rational arithmetic; the generator
  `numerics_check.py` in this directory computes them (60-digit `decimal`, directed rounding) and
  documents the formula.
* For every row of `rows15` and every case (χ₁ complex / χ₁ and ρ₁ real / χ₁ real with ρ₁ complex)
  the file defines the corresponding upper bound `n151_F_*` of `K⁻² Σ_{χ≠χ₀} Σ'_ρ |F((1-ρ)𝓛)|`
  (the value of the right-hand side of HB Lemma 15.1), and proves `n151_F_* < 1` by `norm_num`.
* The list `lemma151Totals` collects them; `lemma151TotalsHB` records the same computation for
  HB's *unshifted* tables.

**Recorded margins** (`1 - worst total`):

| tables | worst total | margin |
|---|---|---|
| HB's printed tables | `≤ 994421/1000000` (`= 0.994421`) | `≥ 5579/1000000 = 0.005579 ≈ 0.0056` |
| the frozen `rows15` (every λ-bound lowered by `0.001`) | `≤ 995578/1000000` (`= 0.995578`) | `≥ 4422/1000000 = 0.004422` |

The worst entry is `λ₁ ∈ [12/25, 289/600]` (the row `[0.48, 0.50]`), case χ₁ complex, at `Λ = 119/125`
for HB's tables (`951/1000` for the shifted rows).

The `def`s `n151_*` are the *values* of the Lemma-15.1 expression; the expression itself is visible
in the body of each `def` (a `let`-chain of the enclosure data followed by the algebraic
combination `tail + n₁·Cst + 2C(λ₂) + Σ_layers`).  The §14 lower bounds are the `g14_*` defs.
-/
